1 --- FIRST EXCERCISE ON JS
ON THE FISRT EXCERSISE OF JS, I LEARNED HOW TO CREATE A FUNCTION AND WORK WITH IT 
BY MAKING IT LOOP THROUGH A WORD AND RETURN TRUE IF THE WORD READS
 THE SAME WAY FROM LEFT TO RIGHT AND RIGHT TO LEFT, AND RETURN FALSE IN THE OPPOSITE SITUATION.
-----------------
2 --- SECOND EXCERSISE ON JS
 ON THE SECOND EXCERSISE, I LEARNED HOW TO USE SPLIT AND LOOP AND UPPERCASE AND 
 HOW TO CREATE AN ACRONYM FROM THE FIRST WORD OF ANY SENTENCE .
------------------
3 --- THIRD EXCERSISE ON JS
 ON THE THIRD EXCERSISE, I LEARNED HOW TO CREATE A FUNCTION WITH TWO PARAMETRES USING +, AND QUOTATION MARKS. 
------------------
4 --- FOURTH EXCERSISE ON JS
ON THE FOURTH EXCERSISE, I LEARNED HOW TO CALCULATE A RECTANGLE, AND HOW TO USE DEFAULT PARAMETRES, 
AND TO AUTOMATICALLY USE A PREDEFINED VALUE. 
-------------------
5 --- FIFTH EXCERSISE ON JS
ON THE FIFTH EXCERSISE, I LEARNED HOW TO USE ARRAYS, FOR LOOPS WITH INDEXES AND LENGTH AND PUSH TO CREATE
AN ARRAY CONTAINING NUMBERS MULTIPLIED BY 2.
-------------------
6 --- SIXTH EXCERSISE ON JS
ON THE SIXTH EXCERSISE, I LEARNED HOW TO REPEAT AN OPERATION FROM 1 UP TO MAX, THEN HOW TO CHECK IF A NUMBER IS DIVISBLE 
BY ANOTHER NUMBER.
-------------------
7 --- SEVENTH EXCERSISE ON JS
ON THE SEVENTH EXCERSISE, I LEARNED HOW TO CONVERT A TIME STRING INTO THE TOTAL NUMBER OF MINUTES SINCE MIDNIGHT.
-------------------
8 --- EIGHTH EXCERSISE ON JS
ON THE EIGHTH EXCERSISE, I LEARNED HOW TO MANIPULATE STRINGS, EXTRACT CHARACHTERS AND CHANGE LETTER CASES THEN COMBINE 
EVERYTHING TO PRODUCE A FORMATTED RESULT. 
-------------------
